2026/11/03: Terminal modernization beta (V1.9.3-beta1).
            Switch channels by left-clicking the lower channel overview in
            local xterm-compatible terminals. Keep terminal text selection
            available through Shift and disable mouse tracking on exit.
            Restore scroll regions without resetting terminal modes, so
            mouse reporting survives initial drawing and screen switches.
            Display INP transport times in milliseconds and mark withdrawn
            routes. Decode TNN L3RTT probes, reported timings and INP
            capability/maximum-time tokens alongside existing RIF options.
            Follow local terminal resizes without losing buffered rows or
            unsent input. Clip existing rows instead of reflowing them and
            scroll long input horizontally. Show a notice below 80x16;
            continue network processing while local keyboard input is paused.
            Define UMLAUT ON as ASCII transliteration (ae/oe/ue/ss) and
            UMLAUT OFF as preserving umlauts, consistently for keyboard,
            receive and log-file conversion. Default to OFF to retain
            umlauts at startup. This reverses the historical ON/OFF meaning.
            Restore Latin-1/IBM umlaut tables.
            Remove the obsolete UTF-8 lead-byte workaround and distinguish
            decoded Alt shortcuts from ordinary high-bit text characters.
            Refresh the channel overview immediately after CONCALL changes.
            Restore Alt-B/Alt-Shift-B mailbox screen shortcuts instead of
            interpreting the internal mailbox key code as text ("ae").
            Use system gettext and checked UTF-8 translation catalogs.
            Match modern xterm/rxvt/screen/tmux terminal profiles.
            Detect color capability, reset intensity correctly and support
            optional indexed/RGB role palettes with reduced-color fallback.
            Add UTF-8 terminal I/O while preserving legacy radio/file bytes.
            Keep the legacy frontend wire format and reject keyboard
            characters that cannot be represented in Latin-1.
            Add sanitizer-backed terminal and color regression tests.

2026/11/03: Fixed signed-char bugs that disabled binary-frame detection,
            control-character display conversion and umlaut upcasing on
            platforms with signed char. Matched status attribute extern
            declarations with their char definitions. Fixed a use-after-free
            when closing an AXSERV socket after a failed write, bounded the
            socket write buffer, chunked oversized frontend buffer writes,
            and plugged descriptor/memory leaks in cookie generation and
            broadcast file conversion. Hardened script comment stripping
            against empty lines.

2026/11/02: Modern C function definitions and complete prototypes.
            Removed legacy compiler-warning suppressions and forced GNU C99.
            Corrected callback signatures, character conversion calls and
            socket argument types. Added sanitizer-backed make check tests.
            Check file and terminal I/O results with fortified builds on all
            CI architectures. Handle interrupted/partial transfers, reject
            unreadable password data, and report read/write failures.
            Correct cookie header/footer lengths and preserve help text at EOF.
            Disable only leak detection under QEMU; retain ASan and UBSan.
            Keep broadcast file IDs and header sizes unsigned on 32-bit builds.
            Use 64-bit directory/file metadata in the run-program help utility
            and report directory scan failures instead of showing an empty list.

2000/06/06: TNT 1.9.1 (added subversion .1 because of the many distributed
		       1.9-versions)

2000/01/06: created CVS repository

1999/09/09: Version 1.9 in development
2026/11/04: TNT V2.0.0-rc1 release candidate.
            Promote the overnight-tested terminal modernization to main.
            Provide Debian 12 amd64/arm64/armhf packages and an openSUSE
            Leap 16 x86_64 RPM with matching source and checksums.
            Packages do not start a service or replace user configurations.
            This remains a release candidate, not a final 2.0 release.
2026/11/04: Fix LOADPRIV for existing connections: refresh channel password
            assignments, discard pending challenges and clear removed entries
            instead of retaining references to freed password records.
            Keep the previous table if a replacement cannot be loaded.
2026/11/04: Refresh the lower channel overview immediately when a received
            connected/reconnected message changes the displayed callsign.
            Do not wait for another received line or keyboard event.
